    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {
        "id": "ZY35yVbAfU9b"
      },
      "source": [
        "## 1) Signal checks\n",
        "\n",
        "**Signal 1: days since last update (refresh flag).** Verdict: **MIXED.** Nearly all pages were updated within the last 23 days (n=2,399), where the label rate is 0.587. The 34 pages 61+ days stale show 0.765, which matches the flag's direction, but the group is small and the 24-60 day bucket (0.591) shows no trend. Directional only.\n",
        "\n",
        "**Signal 2: early-window impressions (quick-win flag).** Verdict: **OPPOSITE.** The label rate falls as volume rises, from 0.662 in the lowest bucket to 0.503 in the highest (n≈505 each). The quick-win logic favours high-volume pages, but in this sample low-volume pages carried the label more often. Part of this may be noise, because low-volume pages have noisier daily clicks and cross a relative-drop threshold more easily.\n",
        "\n",
        "**Extra check: CTR vs peers at the same position (CTR-fix flag).** Verdict: **FALSE.** Flat across buckets (0.570 to 0.626, n≈505 each), so I dropped it from the rule.\n",
        "\n",
        "**What this means for my rule:** the rule leans mainly on low volume, with a small weight on staleness (MIXED, weak). I did not copy the quick-win direction, because the data pointed the other way."
      ],
      "id": "ZY35yVbAfU9b"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": 16,
      "metadata": {
        "id": "sO8nowMDfU9c",
        "colab": {
          "base_uri": "https://localhost:8080/"
        },
        "outputId": "033a29d6-4bea-4bbe-982e-c206c287fcf3"
      },
      "outputs": [
        {
          "output_type": "stream",
          "name": "stdout",
          "text": [
            "(2526, 7) | share label=1: 0.59\n"
          ]
        }
      ],
      "source": [
        "import duckdb, numpy as np, pandas as pd, os, json\n",
        "from huggingface_hub import hf_hub_download\n",
        "from google.colab import userdata\n",
        "\n",
        "TOKEN, REPO = userdata.get(\"HF_TOKEN\"), \"FlyRank/internship-warehouse\"\n",
        "FACT = hf_hub_download(REPO, \"fact_content_daily_performance/month=2026-03/data_0.parquet\", repo_type=\"dataset\", token=TOKEN)\n",
        "DIM_CONTENT = hf_hub_download(REPO, \"dim_content.parquet\", repo_type=\"dataset\", token=TOKEN)\n",
        "con = duckdb.connect()\n",
        "\n",
        "df = con.sql(f\"\"\"\n",
        "WITH early AS (\n",
        "  SELECT client_hash_id, content_hash_id, SUM(gsc_impressions) AS impressions_early,\n",
        "         SUM(gsc_clicks) AS clicks_early, AVG(gsc_avg_position) AS avg_position_early\n",
        "  FROM read_parquet('{FACT}')\n",
        "  WHERE gsc_data_available IS TRUE AND report_date BETWEEN DATE '2026-03-01' AND DATE '2026-03-20'\n",
        "  GROUP BY 1, 2),\n",
        "late AS (\n",
        "  SELECT client_hash_id, content_hash_id, SUM(gsc_clicks) AS clicks_late\n",
        "  FROM read_parquet('{FACT}')\n",
        "  WHERE gsc_data_available IS TRUE AND report_date BETWEEN DATE '2026-03-21' AND DATE '2026-03-31'\n",
        "  GROUP BY 1, 2)\n",
        "SELECT e.client_hash_id, e.content_hash_id, e.impressions_early,\n",
        "       e.clicks_early * 1.0 / NULLIF(e.impressions_early, 0) AS ctr_early,\n",
        "       e.avg_position_early,\n",
        "       DATE '2026-03-20' - c.content_updated_date AS days_since_update,\n",
        "       (COALESCE(l.clicks_late, 0) / 11.0) < 0.8 * (e.clicks_early / 20.0) AS label\n",
        "FROM early e\n",
        "JOIN read_parquet('{DIM_CONTENT}') c USING (client_hash_id, content_hash_id)\n",
        "LEFT JOIN late l USING (client_hash_id, content_hash_id)\n",
        "WHERE e.clicks_early >= 5 AND c.content_updated_date <= DATE '2026-03-20'\n",
        "\"\"\").df()\n",
        "df[\"label\"] = df[\"label\"].astype(int)\n",
        "df[\"days_since_update\"] = df[\"days_since_update\"].astype(float)\n",
        "print(df.shape, \"| share label=1:\", round(df[\"label\"].mean(), 3))"
      ],
      "id": "sO8nowMDfU9c"
    },
